# The CI validate job runs `dotnet build` on the runner before `docker build`, which leaves
# runner-generated obj/ (with project.assets.json pointing at the runner's package folders) in the
# build context. `COPY . ./` then overwrites the restore the build stage just performed, and
# `dotnet publish --no-restore` fails with NETSDK1064 for packages that exist only on the runner.
# Excluding the outputs keeps the image build hermetic whatever ran before it.
bin/
obj/
